  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Evaluating limits of functions (e)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate the value of the following limit:</p>

<p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{x\rightarrow {@0@}}{@eqn@} = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{x\rightarrow {@0@}}{@eqn@} \implies f(x)={@eqn@}\)</p>

 <p>As  \(x\) becomes close to \(0, {@var_2*x ^ var_1@}\)  also  becomes close to \(0\) and \({@eqn@}\) becomes very large.</p>
<p>By taking \(x\) close enough to \(0\) the value of \(f(x)\) doesn't approach a number, so <p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{x\rightarrow {@0@}}{@eqn@}\) does not exist. </p>
<p>Thus we can use the notation \(\displaystyle \lim_{x\rightarrow {@0@}}{@eqn@}={@ta@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
